# MCP SQLite Gemini Bridge

A production-ready local-to-cloud bridge that uses the **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** to give **Google Gemini Enterprise Agents** secure, controlled access to your **local SQLite database**.

## 🎯 Overview

This project solves a critical enterprise challenge: **How do I safely extend my AI agents with access to local data without exposing my infrastructure?**

The bridge acts as a secure intermediary:
- Your local SQLite database stays on your infrastructure
- Gemini Enterprise Agents communicate through encrypted MCP protocol
- Query validation prevents SQL injection and dangerous operations
- Complete audit trail of all access and queries

## 🏗️ Architecture


## ✨ Key Features

### 🔐 Security
- **API Key Authentication** - Hashed & salted keys
- **SQL Injection Prevention** - Query pattern validation & whitelisting
- **Rate Limiting** - Configurable per-minute and per-hour limits
- **TLS/mTLS Support** - End-to-end encryption
- **Audit Trail** - Complete query history with timestamps
- **Blocked Operations** - DROP, DELETE, ALTER, etc. blocked by default

### 🤖 Agent Integration
- **Gemini Enterprise OAuth 2.0** - Secure authentication
- **Session Management** - Maintain conversation context
- **Tool Exposure** - Exposes database operations as callable tools
- **Message History** - Track all agent interactions

### 📊 Operations
- **Connection Pooling** - Efficient SQLite connection management
- **Query Timeouts** - Prevent long-running queries
- **Schema Introspection** - Get database structure information
- **Aggregate Functions** - COUNT, SUM, AVG, MAX, MIN support
- **Comprehensive Logging** - Pino-based structured logging

